1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,563
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,988
[Lily] <i>Helena Montoya's account, please.</i>

6
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:31,614
[man] <i>Security, she's here.</i>

7
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,241
[Lily] <i>Your key doesn't work!</i>

8
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,909
<i>Maybe that's what triggered the alarm!</i>

9
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,077
[Mercedes] <i>This is the correct key.</i>

10
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,913
<i>Unless Lily Cruz might have replaced it.</i>

11
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,499
[Raul] <i>Diego Torillo is here,</i>
<i>in Red Dragon's lair.</i>

12
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:45,211
<i>I want to ask you a favor.</i>
<i>Please take care of the kid.</i>

13
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,756
[Damian] <i>Diego Torillo is a good kid.</i>
<i>You can count on me.</i>

14
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:50,341
<i>Mercedes told me to keep an eye on you,</i>
<i>so don't give me any trouble.</i>

15
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,844
<i>What are you looking at?</i>
<i>Are you curious about what I'm doing?</i>

16
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:55,013
[Diego] <i>I'm studying how</i>
<i>I'm going to replace you.</i>

17
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:58,391
<i>I'm not a lackey like you.</i>
<i>I'm Red Dragon's ally.</i>

18
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,894
<i>Arnaldo! What are you doing?</i>
<i>What's happening to you?!</i>

19
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:03,605
<i>Lily can answer my questions.</i>
<i>I need to talk to her.</i>

20
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>Tell me. What happened? Tell me the truth!</i>

21
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:08,485
<i>You killed my Nanny Carlotta.</i>

22
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:11,112
[Damian] <i>Julio Ardiente's still after you.</i>

23
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:14,657
<i>The violence won't stop,</i>
<i>no matter whose camp you join.</i>

24
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,242
<i>It could be worse for you now</i>

25
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:18,703
<i>since you sided with Red Dragon.</i>

26
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:21,664
[Jepoy] <i>Red Dragon will use</i>
<i>Diego against you, Lily.</i>

27
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:24,918
<i>She could use Diego</i>
<i>against Julio Ardiente.</i>

28
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:25,960
[Diego] <i>What's that for?</i>

29
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:30,548
[Helena] <i>I want you to kill Lily Cruz.</i>

30
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:31,674
<i>Diego.</i>

31
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,635
<i>Here's the blue book.</i>

32
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:35,512
<i>All of Red Dragon's clients</i>
<i>are listed there.</i>

33
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:37,388
<i>I'll have her hideout raided.</i>

34
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:39,849
<i>What's important is we take down</i>
<i>Red Dragon and the Ardientes!</i>

35
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,893
<i>I promise you, I'll be fine.</i>

36
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:44,938
<i>Diego, please.</i>
<i>Don't go back there anymore.</i>

37
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,448
[tense music playing]

38
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,634
-Is this real?
-Yes, Red Dragon.

39
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:15,969
Shut up!

40
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,188
They look legit.

41
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:31,442
According to this website,
Lily Cruz did book a flight.

42
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,738
So, what are you waiting for?

43
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,741
I have a concert to do tonight.

44
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:43,705
Do not disturb me. Go after Lily Cruz!

45
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,082
[tense music playing]

46
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,051
[Julio] Oh!

47
00:02:57,927 --> 00:03:02,932
Criminal case number N17-455…

48
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:09,981
Dismissed based on
lack of witnesses and evidence.

49
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,525
[laughs]

50
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:15,028
The case against me is dismissed.

51
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:16,863
Which means…

52
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:22,410
I will be going back to the capitol

53
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:28,917
to claim my rightful title
as governor of Ardiente!

54
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,378
[laughing]

55
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:35,590
How sweet it is!

56
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:40,178
Great news! Great news, Papa!

57
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:41,679
Yes.

58
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:48,061
But you know what?
Tell that to a garbage bin.

59
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:51,940
That's where you'll find
tons of "plastic!"

60
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:56,194
Look, Papa. I am genuinely happy for you.

61
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:58,488
-[scoffs]
-But you know, Papa?

62
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,990
With all the lawsuits against you,

63
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:04,035
I doubt you'll ever be reinstated.

64
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:05,620
Anything can happen.

65
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:09,749
Oh, yes. Of course. Anything can happen.

66
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:14,420
Including me offering you

67
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:16,965
a position in government.

68
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:20,218
Come on, Papa. Save the sweet talk.

69
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,678
You never offered me anything.

70
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:25,390
In fact, you're the reason
I was removed from power,

71
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:29,477
whereas Mama offered me a seat
in her group.

72
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,604
And with all the lawsuits
and controversies

73
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:33,189
surrounding your victory,

74
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:36,484
I doubt you'll be reinstated as governor.

75
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,028
So, don't count your chickens
before they hatch, Papa.

76
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:41,948
[scoffs] We'll see.

77
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:48,162
But suddenly, I just came up
with the greatest idea.

78
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:49,664
The brightest one at that.

79
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:56,546
I know the perfect affair where
I will declare my reinstatement.

80
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:01,843
And it's going to happen with a bang!

81
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,654
[tense music playing]

82
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:30,705
Ridiculous. This is impossible, Attorney.

83
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:34,542
Julio Ardiente can't be reinstated.

84
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,461
This is not the end of it.

85
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:38,588
So, that's it?

86
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:43,593
Everything we've done to oust
Julio Ardiente was for nothing?

87
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:45,845
Our efforts just went down the drain?

88
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,849
What would Lily say?

89
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:54,604
We'll review this, Camia.
This is not over.

90
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:58,858
No, Attorney. Diego was right.

91
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:01,819
Let's stop fighting the clean way.

92
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:04,197
Helena Montoya has a concert tonight.

93
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,657
I'm sure Julio Ardiente will be there.

94
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,827
We'll fight for the truth there.

95
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,880
Mama, the case was dismissed.

96
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:25,218
Relax. Your father hasn't
been reinstated yet.

97
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:28,888
Mama, you know how he works.
He's got connections.

98
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,766
He can easily get off the hook. Besides,

99
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:35,394
he said he'll make us kneel
once he becomes the governor.

100
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,938
[chuckles]

101
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:40,817
Emilia, my princess.
Don't be such a worrier.

102
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:44,779
Nothing's happened yet.
You're dampening my spirits.

103
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:50,618
Well, if it's war that your father wants,

104
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,788
it's war that I'm going to give him.

105
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:04,006
Please take them to the car, okay?

106
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:04,924
Yes, ma'am.

107
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:14,600
-Love.
-Yes?

108
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:18,354
Maybe it's better if you just stay here.

109
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:20,148
Don't come with us.

110
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:24,944
I can't, love. I need to go
to Auntie Camia's protest.

111
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:26,988
Something might happen.

112
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:29,031
I don't want you to get hurt.
Just stay here.

113
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,619
I didn't know you were
a strict boyfriend, Jepoy.

114
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,997
But with everything
that's been happening lately,

115
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,875
I have to be there for them.
So, don't worry.

116
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:44,505
I can take care of myself.
You'll be there too, right?

117
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:49,051
Shouldn't you be supporting me
in our fight?

118
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:54,140
Remember, you're one
of the people Lily can count on.

119
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:57,852
Okay, fine, fine.

120
00:07:58,227 --> 00:07:59,896
Please allow me to go.

121
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:04,692
Just don't leave my side, okay?

122
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,778
I won't.

123
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:09,697
-Promise?
-Promise.

124
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:17,747
[tense music playing]

125
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:34,388
[tense music continues playing]

126
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,822
[tense music continues playing]

127
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:00,957
What is it, love? Is something wrong?

128
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:03,751
I just feel like…

129
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:07,880
someone's watching us.

130
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:08,965
Where?

131
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:19,100
That's right, Anna.
You should be very afraid.

132
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,938
Because you're my next target.

133
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:29,902
Are you ready?

134
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:44,709
It's probably nothing.

135
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:49,338
You should stop being paranoid, love.

136
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:53,968
As long as you're with me,
you'll always be safe.

137
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:05,021
[groans]

138
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:10,818
Damn it, Jepoy.
What did you see in that woman?

139
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:15,865
Can't you see that she is obviously

140
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,117
a total downgrade from me?

141
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,494
Can't you see that?

142
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,293
I'd get it if she satisfies your needs.

143
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:30,630
Which I assume she doesn't.

144
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:38,387
Natalie, what the hell are you doing here?

145
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,431
What the hell is going on?

146
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:45,853
Can you just stop? You're going insane.

147
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,190
You just need a distraction, Natalie.

148
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,275
That's all you need.

149
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:53,235
Just stop.

150
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:11,587
Red Dragon, huh?

151
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,969
I've been wanting to join
your group for a while now.

152
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:28,813
Well, why don't I stop thinking
about it and just do it?

153
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:41,909
[crowd cheering]

154
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:45,496
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you!

155
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:49,500
Thank you. I'm glad to be back!
Thank you very much!

156
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:53,003
Thank you to all of you.
Thank you very much.

157
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:57,800
-What are you doing here?
-Oh, good morning.

158
00:11:57,883 --> 00:12:00,386
Actually, I should be the one
asking you that question.

159
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:03,097
What are you doing here?

160
00:12:04,014 --> 00:12:05,975
Security, why did you let him in?

161
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:07,977
Apprehend him!

162
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,899
It's all right, boys. Stay.

163
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:15,693
Sit.

164
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:17,445
Behave.

165
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:22,158
I don't think your
security force has the right

166
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:25,369
nor the power to remove me
from this premises

167
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:30,416
because you are now talking
to the newly reinstated

168
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:36,005
governor of this place we call home.

169
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:38,257
The decision is not yet official.

170
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:42,386
Ah! Official, official, my foot.

171
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:46,348
All that's missing is the date
of my reinstatement.

172
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:50,686
And so, it's official when I say so.

173
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:54,190
And today, in front
of all these witnesses.

174
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:58,360
That's why it's official. Isn't it?

175
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:05,201
Oh, by the way, I noticed you
were on your way to <i>my</i> office.

176
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:10,748
I think your office
is way on the other side.

177
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,208
Because I remembered passing by,

178
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:14,502
and I saw it was written on the door.

179
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:18,214
"Vice Governor Mateo".

180
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:21,759
And down here
is the office of the governor,

181
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:25,679
which is me, Julio Ardiente.

182
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,057
You know, Mateo?

183
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:35,689
As far as I can remember,
I never rented out my seat.

184
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:38,108
I didn't lease it out.

185
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:42,613
The governor's chair
belongs to me and me alone.

186
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:46,408
It's mine. It's very much mine.

187
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:51,372
And I don't feel like
sharing it with anyone.

188
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:53,958
So, I would suggest
you go back to your office,

189
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:55,376
I will be in my office,

190
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:59,129
and should there be any need
for us to talk further,

191
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,215
I will call for you.

192
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:03,926
Don't call me. I'll call you.

193
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:06,345
Okay, Vice?

194
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:08,847
I'll see you around.

195
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:16,605
[Julio] Arnaldo!

196
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:20,276
Arnaldo, my grandson!

197
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,444
Your grandpa is here!

198
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:25,072
I've got good news for you.

199
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:27,199
Come on!

200
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:31,537
Arnaldo, get changed! We're going out!

201
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:35,541
We're going to watch a concert
and celebrate.

202
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:41,422
Because your grandpa, the king
of Ardiente, is back on top!

203
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:43,132
[Julio laughs]

204
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:46,510
-What the-- Nico!
-Yes, Governor.

205
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,638
-What happened?
-Governor, it's Mayor Arnaldo!

206
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:52,808
Arnaldo!

207
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:54,393
Arnaldo!

208
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:56,687
-Arnaldo!
-Mayor Arnaldo!

209
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:57,980
Arnaldo!

210
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,400
Arnaldo, wake up!

211
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:03,527
What happened to you?

212
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,740
Look at you. You look like dirt.

213
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:09,992
Well? What happened to you?

214
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:15,122
Arnaldo, I'm talking to you.

215
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:18,459
Grandpa, it's…

216
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:24,214
-It's Lily.
-Huh?

217
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:25,841
Lily said…

218
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:29,219
Lily said I killed her Nanny Carlotta.

219
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:34,433
Is that true? Did I do that?

220
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:35,768
Huh?

221
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,561
-No.
-Did I kill her?

222
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:41,482
-Am I a bad person?
-No. You are not a bad person.

223
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:44,276
-And this stops now!
-Am I bad?

224
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,487
I did not kill…

225
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:50,157
I killed someone. But I'm not a killer.

226
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,283
No. No.

227
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:55,621
I'm not a killer.
I'm not a killer. I'm not.

228
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,959
That's enough. This has to stop.

229
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:03,462
It's time for you to come home.

230
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:06,215
You'll come to the mansion
whether you like it or not.

231
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,218
-Why would I kill…
-Nico, help him up.

232
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:10,260
Yes, sir.

233
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,929
-Mayor.
-Stand up!

234
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:16,517
This place smells like crap!

235
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:20,604
Come on! Let's take him home.

236
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:24,400
Let's go.

237
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:30,197
Let's leave this… I don't know
what to call this place!

238
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:39,707
[tense music playing]

239
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:56,807
Everyone listen.

240
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:59,184
These are the weapons we'll be using

241
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:01,395
at Madam Red Dragon's concert.

242
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:04,732
Diego, Romulo.

243
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:10,487
This is the list of targets
Red Dragon invited,

244
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:14,074
who could be the keys to Julio
Ardiente's reinstatement.

245
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:18,162
We will dispatch them all. Understand?

246
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:21,665
[Diego] All of them?

247
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:24,877
We'll kill all of them?

248
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:27,796
Well, if Red Dragon says kill them all,

249
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,089
we kill them all.

250
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:31,258
[tense music playing]

251
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:35,846
Double-check the blue book, Romulo.

252
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:38,599
If Red Dragon's allies show up,

253
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:41,727
seat them all together,
away from where we'll open fire.

254
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,813
[upbeat music playing]

255
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,443
<i>Where's Diego? Diego!</i>

256
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:51,904
<i>Put that down!</i>

257
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:53,197
[thuds]

258
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:56,742
<i>I'm sorry. I thought it was mine.</i>

259
00:17:58,285 --> 00:18:00,537
Diego, where's the blue book?

260
00:18:00,954 --> 00:18:03,373
[tense music playing]

261
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,217
Is this what you're looking for?

262
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,263
Where did you get that?

263
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:22,392
Unlike you, I know how to
keep things safe and hidden.

264
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:34,780
Diego made a copy of the blue
book before he gave it to me.

265
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,699
We can use that, dear.

266
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,995
But, Lily, what's your plan?

267
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:46,875
Diego said Red Dragon alerted the airport,

268
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:50,671
the same airport
where they think you'll be.

269
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:55,884
Red Dragon's people are probably
on their way there right now.

270
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,846
Don't worry about it, Mom.

271
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:02,766
I alerted the police
about the entrapment operation.

272
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,894
When the Dragon Ladies get there,

273
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:06,979
they're ours.

274
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:13,110
Okay, but what will happen at
Helena Montoya's event tonight?

275
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:17,197
[tense music playing]

276
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:35,340
Hello, Miss Mercedes.

277
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:40,345
-Who the hell are you?
-I'm Natalie.

278
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:46,643
And you are Mercedes Palacio.
Am I correct?

279
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:52,441
I have no time to be chatting
with strangers.

280
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:53,901
Let's go.

281
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,736
Hang on, wait. Um…

282
00:19:56,695 --> 00:20:00,282
Well, actually, it's okay
if you don't know who I am.

283
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,619
What's important is I know who you are.

284
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:05,829
I did my research.

285
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:11,210
And I know your dirty little secret.

286
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:12,961
[chuckles]

287
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,922
I know who you work for.

288
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:20,135
You work for the queen, Red Dragon?

289
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:23,680
Am I right?

290
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:26,767
Please get this woman out of my way.

291
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:28,018
Uh-uh!

292
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:29,394
[chuckles]

293
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:30,771
Don't touch me.

294
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:34,733
I didn't come here as your enemy.

295
00:20:35,442 --> 00:20:38,195
I came here as your ally.

296
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:44,826
And, possibly, we can work together.

297
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:49,831
I have a lot of money
and I have the resources.

298
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:54,336
All I need is a meeting with your boss.

299
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:59,007
And I'm sure she'd be
interested in working with me.

300
00:20:59,716 --> 00:21:01,009
So, make it happen.

301
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:03,553
[chuckles]

302
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:05,931
I think you're lost, Miss…

303
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:11,979
Whatever your name is.

304
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:16,441
First off, I'm not involved
with this "Red Dragon."

305
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:20,112
Second, I'm not involved in the sex trade.

306
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:21,363
Excuse me?

307
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,991
So, if you're trying to apply
as a prostitute,

308
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:25,993
go online.

309
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:28,829
Sluts are high-tech nowadays.

310
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:33,041
With that said, you can either
leave on your own,

311
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:35,419
or I'll have those two
drag you out of here.

312
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:36,586
Goodbye.

313
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:41,925
I'll be seeing you again, Mercedes.

314
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:45,762
[chuckles]

315
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,149
[Mercedes] Let's go.

316
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:00,527
Mercedes.

317
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:05,866
Mr. Oscar. What a surprise.
How did you find me?

318
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,367
I have my ways.

319
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,078
[Mercedes] Well, what brought
you here, sir?

320
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:12,205
I need to talk to… you know who.

321
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:13,874
Oh, Mr. Oscar.

322
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:16,168
The Madam is quite busy at the moment.

323
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:19,379
But I can set an appointment
so you two can talk.

324
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:24,217
The NBI raided my operations.
I lost millions.

325
00:22:24,801 --> 00:22:26,720
And that's why I need
to talk to the Madam.

326
00:22:27,345 --> 00:22:29,389
Sir Oscar, just relax.

327
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:31,558
The Madam will find a way out of this.

328
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,643
I'll just call you, okay?

329
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:35,937
Let's go.

330
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:03,340
[Mercedes] So you have to take note of
every instruction I give you.

331
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:04,925
-Let's go? Come.
-Okay.

332
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,635
[easy music playing]

333
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,472
[no audible dialogue]

334
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:13,642
Okay, so, as we discussed
at the briefing earlier,

335
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:16,603
you will have your designated
posts inside the venue.

336
00:23:16,686 --> 00:23:19,815
I need you to be in your
individual positions as planned.

337
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:22,275
-Is that clear?
-Yes, ma'am.

338
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:23,944
-Okay. You may go.
-Yes, ma'am.

339
00:23:28,532 --> 00:23:30,117
Miss Cruz, why are you sabotaging

340
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,119
Miss Helena Montoya's benefit concert?

341
00:23:32,202 --> 00:23:34,996
The Ardientes are just using that concert

342
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,624
to cover up major issues,

343
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:40,335
such as the pending cases
against Julio Ardiente.

344
00:23:40,418 --> 00:23:45,006
He's been charged with homicide,
theft, and electoral fraud.

345
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:47,551
So, there's no way
we're going to let him reign

346
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:50,053
as governor ever again.

347
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,778
[tense music playing]

348
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:17,747
Well, Madam Emilia, you are looking good.

349
00:24:17,831 --> 00:24:20,083
Your gown brings out your eyes.

350
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:22,502
Thank you, Mercedes.

351
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:24,171
But I know you're just saying that

352
00:24:24,254 --> 00:24:26,089
because you want to gain
back my Mama's favor,

353
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:28,842
now that I'm her right-hand woman.

354
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:32,512
So, with that, you have to obey
every word that I tell you.

355
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:36,183
Actually, just for this event.
Not for the entire operation.

356
00:24:36,266 --> 00:24:37,434
Oh, no.

357
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:40,187
For this event and… suspiciously,

358
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:41,938
why isn't Lily Cruz here?

359
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:45,108
As a matter of fact, I know
she's flying out of the country,

360
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:47,485
and my people are already after her.

361
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:48,570
[scoffs]

362
00:24:49,112 --> 00:24:53,950
Mercedes, Mama did make the
right decision to replace you.

363
00:24:54,034 --> 00:24:56,203
You are silly and naïve.

364
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:59,831
How could you believe her
when she said she was leaving?

365
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:03,793
She fooled us before, remember?
Everyone thought she was dead.

366
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:06,379
But look at her now. She's still alive.

367
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:10,342
So, if I were you, Mercedes,
I wouldn't believe her

368
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:15,764
when she says she's already
making her way to the airport

369
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:19,017
because she could just be
setting you all up.

370
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:20,936
Piece of advice.

371
00:25:21,019 --> 00:25:23,396
As long as you haven't seen her
boarding the plane

372
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,149
with your own eyes,

373
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:29,027
don't believe that she's leaving.

374
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,364
Because Lily Cruz never flees.

375
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:35,951
And more importantly, she never dies.

376
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,328
Excuse me.

377
00:25:38,411 --> 00:25:41,039
[tense music playing]

378
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:07,649
[suspenseful music playing]

379
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:09,276
[indistinct chatter]

380
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,157
Please, be seated inside.

381
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:17,784
Hello.

382
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:19,494
There are seats inside just for you.

383
00:26:19,869 --> 00:26:21,288
Please, be seated inside.

384
00:26:21,371 --> 00:26:22,414
Good evening.

385
00:26:22,789 --> 00:26:23,790
Hi!

386
00:26:27,168 --> 00:26:28,253
Enjoy the show.

387
00:26:30,797 --> 00:26:33,091
[suspenseful music playing]

388
00:26:39,806 --> 00:26:41,766
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

389
00:26:49,607 --> 00:26:50,608
Diego.

390
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:57,407
I'm trying to get an update
from the Dragon Ladies

391
00:26:57,490 --> 00:27:00,535
I sent to the airport.
They aren't picking up.

392
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:04,039
Okay. I'll cover for you here.

393
00:27:18,845 --> 00:27:21,348
[ominous music playing]

394
00:27:32,025 --> 00:27:34,444
[suspenseful music playing]

395
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:36,821
Arnaldo, my son.

396
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:39,199
Wow! Look at you. You look so great.

397
00:27:39,574 --> 00:27:42,577
Are you okay now? Are you feeling better?

398
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:44,412
-Yeah.
-I'm okay. I'm okay.

399
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:47,707
-He was able to rest at home.
-That's good to know.

400
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:48,708
Um…

401
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:51,002
I still have a lot of questions,
but Grandpa said,

402
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:53,380
if I came tonight,
I might get some answers.

403
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:55,799
Yes, that's right.

404
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:58,218
And you'll finally get to bond
with your grandmother.

405
00:27:58,301 --> 00:27:59,677
Isn't that lovely?

406
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:05,475
-I guess.
-So, shall we go?

407
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:17,070
[Magbanua] Governor, wait.

408
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:19,239
The protest they were planning…

409
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:20,698
Camia Cruz went through with it.

410
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:22,867
[scoffs]

411
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:25,620
-Thank you, Miss Cruz.
-Thank you.

412
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:29,082
Camia, is there anything I can do to help?

413
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:33,837
We've got it covered.
But thank you for coming.

414
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,464
I'll do anything for you and Lily.

415
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:39,926
Don't mind them.

416
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:43,763
They can't stop me
from getting my position back.

417
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:50,145
Women like Camia Cruz
are only good for housework.

418
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:55,734
Cooking, doing the laundry,
taking care of children.

419
00:28:56,776 --> 00:29:01,698
But when it comes to politics,
I'll swallow her whole.

420
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:03,616
Let's go.

421
00:29:04,576 --> 00:29:05,660
[chuckles]

422
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:20,341
[tense music playing]

423
00:29:37,066 --> 00:29:39,694
[tense music intensifies]

424
00:29:54,834 --> 00:29:58,463
[protesters] Step down, Julio Ardiente!

425
00:29:58,546 --> 00:30:01,758
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

426
00:30:01,841 --> 00:30:05,345
Step down, Julio Ardiente!

427
00:30:05,428 --> 00:30:08,723
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

428
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:12,143
Step down, Julio Ardiente!

429
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:15,396
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

430
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:18,817
Step down, Julio Ardiente!

431
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:22,403
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

432
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:25,782
Step down, Julio Ardiente!

433
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,076
[protesters continue chanting]

434
00:30:33,498 --> 00:30:35,959
[phone buzzing]

435
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:46,636
Diego, listen carefully.

436
00:30:46,719 --> 00:30:49,097
[protesters continue chanting]

437
00:30:52,141 --> 00:30:54,310
[tense music playing]

438
00:31:10,493 --> 00:31:11,995
[phone buzzing]

439
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:17,584
[tense music playing]

440
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:37,353
[tense music playing]

441
00:31:41,524 --> 00:31:42,650
[knocks]

442
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,118
[sighs]

443
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:24,359
[Emilia] Mama!

444
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:26,903
-Look at you. You are so…
-Emilia!

445
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:27,987
…beautiful, Mama!

446
00:32:28,696 --> 00:32:30,615
-Thank you.
-Everything's ready.

447
00:32:30,698 --> 00:32:32,116
So, they're all waiting for you.

448
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,202
That's great, darling.

449
00:32:34,869 --> 00:32:37,288
-So, are you ready, Mama?
-Yes, I am.

450
00:32:37,372 --> 00:32:39,248
-Okay. I shall cue them.
-Okay.

451
00:32:39,332 --> 00:32:41,167
-I'll wait for you inside, Mama.
-Great.

452
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:42,710
-Break a leg, Mama!
-Thank you, Emilia.

453
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:44,087
-You're so beautiful.
-Thank you.

454
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:45,546
See you around, Mama.

455
00:32:46,005 --> 00:32:47,006
[Helena sighs]

456
00:32:49,384 --> 00:32:50,843
Is this confirmed?

457
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:54,263
[suspenseful music playing]

458
00:32:58,309 --> 00:33:00,436
[phone ringing]

459
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:04,357
-Hello, Mercedes?
-<i>Madam…</i>

460
00:33:04,899 --> 00:33:07,276
The Dragon Ladies have been
arrested by the police.

461
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:08,486
What?!

462
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:10,279
They are questioning them about you.

463
00:33:10,363 --> 00:33:12,448
They already know you're Red Dragon.

464
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:23,668
[tense music playing]

465
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:55,116
[Emilia] Tonight, we are
celebrating the anniversary

466
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:58,870
of Helena Montoya's Foundation
with music and magic.

467
00:33:58,953 --> 00:34:02,665
With her friends and
beneficiaries of her foundation,

468
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:05,084
without further ado, let's welcome

469
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:07,587
the one and only Helena Montoya.

470
00:34:07,670 --> 00:34:10,256
[applause]

471
00:34:15,178 --> 00:34:18,723
["Maging Sino Ka Man"
instrumental playing]

472
00:35:55,695 --> 00:35:59,949
I just can't believe you let
the Dragon Ladies get arrested.

473
00:36:00,449 --> 00:36:03,494
You know, you're ruining
Mama's special night.

474
00:36:04,453 --> 00:36:05,580
Shut up, Emilia,

475
00:36:05,663 --> 00:36:08,791
if you don't want me to take
my frustration out on you.

476
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:10,877
Wow! [chuckles]

477
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:15,923
You just fell into Lily's trap.
You really are stupid.

478
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:31,457
[applause]

479
00:37:40,716 --> 00:37:42,969
Please, sit down. Please, sit down.

480
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:45,805
Thank you very much.

481
00:37:47,515 --> 00:37:50,309
[ominous music]

482
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:53,396
[tense music playing]

483
00:38:00,152 --> 00:38:01,028
[grunts]

484
00:38:01,654 --> 00:38:02,655
[groans]

485
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:13,874
[Helena] Hello. Good evening, friends.

486
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:16,544
It is such an honor to be in the presence

487
00:38:16,627 --> 00:38:19,005
of very prestigious guests.

488
00:38:19,088 --> 00:38:21,507
And I must say that I am deeply honored,

489
00:38:21,590 --> 00:38:25,428
and I am humbled,
not only by your presence,

490
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:29,348
but of your gift of love and generosity.

491
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:33,602
This night is especially for
the people of Ardiente

492
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:39,525
because all proceeds from this event
will go straight to them.

493
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:44,447
So, thank you so much for your
very early Christmas gift.

494
00:38:44,530 --> 00:38:46,866
Give yourselves a round of applause.

495
00:38:46,949 --> 00:38:49,368
[applause]

496
00:38:53,914 --> 00:38:56,667
I would also like to thank
my special guests.

497
00:38:57,585 --> 00:39:01,672
Business tycoon Salvador Tatad.

498
00:39:01,756 --> 00:39:03,799
Let's all give him a big hand.

499
00:39:03,883 --> 00:39:06,135
[applause]

500
00:39:06,218 --> 00:39:09,055
Former senator Isagani Bacaro.

501
00:39:09,138 --> 00:39:12,016
[applause]

502
00:39:12,099 --> 00:39:15,144
And former ambassador Horacio Perez.

503
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,896
[applause]

504
00:39:16,979 --> 00:39:19,982
Thank you all very much for
making this evening possible.

505
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:25,071
And, of course, I'd like to thank
my only daughter,

506
00:39:26,614 --> 00:39:28,616
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

507
00:39:28,699 --> 00:39:30,201
Let's all give her a big hand too.

508
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:34,246
She single-handedly
organized tonight's event.

509
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:35,706
Thank you very much.

510
00:39:36,540 --> 00:39:38,167
You are the reason

511
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:43,422
for my calling to help
the people of Ardiente.

512
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:51,722
And, finally, the reason
we are all here this evening.

513
00:39:52,306 --> 00:39:57,436
To the one with an unbreakable spirit

514
00:39:58,104 --> 00:40:01,690
and a very passionate heart.

515
00:40:02,817 --> 00:40:05,486
To the one whose name
will never be forgotten.

516
00:40:08,823 --> 00:40:13,619
Ladies and gentlemen, I recognize the one,

517
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:14,870
the only…

518
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:23,712
[ominous music playing]

519
00:40:34,014 --> 00:40:36,642
[upbeat music playing]

520
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:56,287
[upbeat music continues playing]

521
00:41:15,848 --> 00:41:17,224
Lily Cruz.

522
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,939
Oh, yes. I am the one.

523
00:41:24,273 --> 00:41:25,816
The only one.

524
00:41:26,942 --> 00:41:28,944
Lily, what are you doing here?

525
00:41:32,072 --> 00:41:33,240
In just a few seconds,

526
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:37,077
you're all about to receive
a message on your phones.

527
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:44,710
And these messages will reveal
Helena Montoya's true identity.

528
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:51,133
[tense music playing]

529
00:41:57,765 --> 00:42:00,392
[phones chiming]

530
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:08,067
<i>I'm one of the Dragon Ladies</i>

531
00:42:08,150 --> 00:42:10,069
<i>who worked for Red Dragon's organization.</i>

532
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:14,073
<i>And, I guarantee you,</i>

533
00:42:14,615 --> 00:42:19,161
<i>that Red Dragon is none other</i>
<i>than Helena Montoya.</i>

534
00:42:27,169 --> 00:42:29,713
[tense music playing]

535
00:42:39,723 --> 00:42:41,433
-What's going on?
-Mama.

536
00:42:43,269 --> 00:42:46,188
<i>Red Dragon's organization possesses</i>

537
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:48,857
<i>over 50 billion pesos worth of assets.</i>

538
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:53,320
<i>Though, we all know her more</i>
<i>by the name, Helena Montoya.</i>

539
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:56,865
<i>Her organization thrives</i>
<i>on the support of her clients,</i>

540
00:42:56,949 --> 00:42:59,201
<i>who also hide behind masks.</i>

541
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:01,787
[dramatic music]

542
00:43:07,001 --> 00:43:12,590
<i>Her number one client is none</i>
<i>other than Salvador Tatad,</i>

543
00:43:12,673 --> 00:43:17,636
<i>a businessman who acts as a</i>
<i>middleman for terrorist groups.</i>

544
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:23,684
<i>Her next client is Isagani Bacaro.</i>

545
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:29,732
Stop it! Stop this nonsense!
Mercedes, please do something.

546
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:37,281
Why are you laughing?
Why aren't you helping us?

547
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:39,617
You know, you don't really care for us.

548
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:42,161
Why should I care?

549
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:46,332
No one cared for me
when I was in the gutters.

550
00:43:47,374 --> 00:43:52,421
Well, now that you're talking
to the most powerful man

551
00:43:52,504 --> 00:43:53,922
in the land of Ardiente,

552
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:56,383
I couldn't care less about you
and your mother.

553
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:58,719
I wouldn't even lift a finger,

554
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:01,263
even if it meant
your life was on the line.

555
00:44:02,264 --> 00:44:04,308
"Most powerful man in Ardiente?"

556
00:44:04,391 --> 00:44:05,517
What are you talking about?

557
00:44:05,601 --> 00:44:07,394
[laughs]

558
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:09,647
Emilia, Emilia.

559
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:13,192
The answer's so close,
it's about to bite you.

560
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:19,907
I am the new governor of this province.

561
00:44:21,909 --> 00:44:25,329
That's right.
You don't have to be surprised.

562
00:44:26,372 --> 00:44:30,501
And today is the day of my reinstatement.

563
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:33,796
Sorry to steal the thunder
from your mother.

564
00:44:33,879 --> 00:44:39,968
While I'm on my way up,
she's sinking all the way down.

565
00:44:40,344 --> 00:44:42,096
Isn't life amazing?

566
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:45,432
Just a few months ago, I was down and out.

567
00:44:45,516 --> 00:44:47,976
Now, I'm up and about.
Down and out. Up and about.

568
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:49,561
Down and out. Up and about.

569
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:52,106
That rhymes!

570
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:55,109
Don't you feel the itch, you…

571
00:44:57,528 --> 00:45:01,573
No, I wouldn't call you that.
You're my daughter! I love you.

572
00:45:01,657 --> 00:45:02,741
[laughs]

573
00:45:02,825 --> 00:45:03,700
Excuse me.

574
00:45:04,743 --> 00:45:05,744
Arnaldo?

575
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:12,751
Don't look at me.

576
00:45:13,710 --> 00:45:15,003
Well, Helena!

577
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:19,007
Welcome to my world!

578
00:45:20,217 --> 00:45:25,013
It's the kind that can't stand
criminals like you.

579
00:45:25,097 --> 00:45:28,976
[tense music playing]

580
00:45:36,984 --> 00:45:39,194
[breathing heavily]

581
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:06,722
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

582
00:46:08,974 --> 00:46:11,351
Who-- Who are you?

583
00:46:22,946 --> 00:46:24,490
Who are you?

584
00:46:26,742 --> 00:46:28,160
Who the hell are you?

585
00:46:33,415 --> 00:46:34,541
<i>You bastard!</i>

586
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:35,959
<i>You monster!</i>

587
00:46:37,127 --> 00:46:38,921
[gunshots]

588
00:46:39,213 --> 00:46:41,173
[indistinct shouting]

589
00:46:41,256 --> 00:46:42,591
<i>Stand back! Get him!</i>

590
00:46:42,674 --> 00:46:44,426
<i>Now, tell me the truth.</i>

591
00:46:44,885 --> 00:46:48,680
<i>-Answer me!</i>
<i>-Yes! I am!</i>

592
00:46:48,764 --> 00:46:50,641
<i>I am Lily Cruz!</i>

593
00:46:52,684 --> 00:46:54,853
<i>I am Lily Cruz!</i>

594
00:46:54,937 --> 00:46:57,481
<i>I am Lily Cruz! I am Lily Cruz!</i>

595
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:00,901
Lily?

596
00:47:04,571 --> 00:47:07,157
-[chuckles] <i>Ivy.</i>
<i>-Lily Cruz.</i>

597
00:47:07,241 --> 00:47:08,992
<i>-That's my name.</i>
<i>-No. It's Ivy Aguas.</i>

598
00:47:09,076 --> 00:47:10,494
<i>It's Lily Cruz.</i>

599
00:47:10,953 --> 00:47:12,246
Lily Cruz.

600
00:47:15,874 --> 00:47:18,710
Did you have something to do
with what happened to me?

601
00:47:28,220 --> 00:47:30,305
[sighs]

602
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:49,616
What are you doing here?
Why aren't you inside?

603
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:52,369
[tense music playing]

604
00:47:53,662 --> 00:47:57,249
What about you? What are you doing here?

605
00:47:58,292 --> 00:48:02,421
I knew it.
There's something off about you.

606
00:48:03,297 --> 00:48:04,715
What are you up to?

607
00:48:04,798 --> 00:48:06,758
What do you want from Red Dragon?

608
00:48:08,343 --> 00:48:11,013
[tense music playing]

609
00:48:13,181 --> 00:48:16,893
You know what? You have a marvelous voice.

610
00:48:17,394 --> 00:48:19,146
You're a great singer.

611
00:48:19,229 --> 00:48:22,524
But I think you're a better actress

612
00:48:22,608 --> 00:48:25,402
in a "playing innocent" role.

613
00:48:25,944 --> 00:48:29,656
But I regret to tell you,
your show is over.

614
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:33,744
Curtain call!
The jig is up because right now,

615
00:48:34,494 --> 00:48:39,833
everyone here knows that Helena Montoya

616
00:48:39,916 --> 00:48:43,337
is none other than Red Dragon.

617
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:45,631
[mouthing] What?

618
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:49,092
[tense music playing]

619
00:48:49,176 --> 00:48:51,470
[inaudible]

620
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:04,107
[ominous music swelling]

621
00:49:10,781 --> 00:49:15,285
<i>I will not allow someone</i>
<i>like Lily Cruz to slander me.</i>

622
00:49:15,369 --> 00:49:17,537
<i>This Lily Cruz just did it.</i>

623
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:19,456
[Asuncion] <i>Helena Montoya,</i>
<i>you are under arrest</i>

624
00:49:19,539 --> 00:49:22,042
<i>for arms trafficking</i>
<i>and human trafficking.</i>

625
00:49:22,125 --> 00:49:23,460
<i>-Please come with us.</i>
<i>-Wait! Wait!</i>

626
00:49:23,543 --> 00:49:25,212
<i>-You cannot do this to my Mama!</i>
<i>-Let go of me!</i>

627
00:49:25,295 --> 00:49:27,589
[Julio] <i>The mother and her daughter,</i>

628
00:49:27,673 --> 00:49:31,760
<i>both taken down by a wildflower.</i>

629
00:49:31,843 --> 00:49:34,179
<i>Looks like you have something</i>
<i>planned for Lily Cruz.</i>

630
00:49:34,262 --> 00:49:35,389
<i>I am above the law.</i>

631
00:49:35,472 --> 00:49:37,474
<i>No, wait. I am the law.</i>

632
00:49:37,557 --> 00:49:41,186
<i>And that Lily Cruz just declared</i>
<i>a full-fledged war</i>

633
00:49:41,269 --> 00:49:42,896
<i>against Red Dragon.</i>

634
00:49:43,522 --> 00:49:45,816
[theme music playing]
